# lychee ignore patterns — regex matched against the URL.
#
# Ported from the reference template (issue #115, R5) and extended with the
# hosts this repository actually links to.
#
# Every entry is a false positive: a URL that is correct but that a link
# checker cannot verify - login-gated, rate-limited, bot-blocked, or served
# over TLS lychee will not negotiate. A URL that is genuinely broken belongs in
# the diff, not in this file; the first run of this gate found 111 of those and
# every one was fixed. Each pattern below carries the reason it is here.

# Localhost and local development URLs
http://localhost
https://localhost
http://127\.0\.0\.1
https://127\.0\.0\.1

# Example/placeholder URLs commonly used in documentation
https://example\.com
http://example\.com

# npmjs.com returns 403 to link checkers (bot protection)
https://www\.npmjs\.com

# medium.com returns 403 to link checkers (bot protection)
https://medium\.com

# web.archive.org returns 502 to link checkers (bot protection)
https://web\.archive\.org

# GitHub repository settings pages require admin authentication; an anonymous
# GET is 404 by design, for a URL the maintainer needs and that is correct.
https://github\.com/[^/]+/[^/]+/settings/

# Docker Hub account settings redirect to the login flow, which lychee follows
# in a loop and rejects. Same reason as the GitHub settings pages above.
https://hub\.docker\.com/settings/

# manpages.ubuntu.com answers 503 under any load, and gnu.org rate-limits
# link checkers with 429. Both hosts are correct; their availability is not.
https://manpages\.ubuntu\.com
https://www\.gnu\.org

# flatassembler.net offers no TLS suite lychee's rustls build will negotiate
# ("received fatal alert: HandshakeFailure"). The site is up in a browser.
https://(arm\.)?flatassembler\.net
